
Optimized procedure for obtaining free energies of hydration for a molecule.
The molecule is annihilated in the gas-phase and in water at 25 C.

The molecule's zmatrix molecule.z needs to be in the boss/molecules/OPLS2020 directory.

Then, execute 

xDGHYD molecule

This script creates a subdirectory molecule and runs a series of jobs:
It first creates z-matrices for the charge and LJ annihilations. 
It then submits 4 FEP jobs with 20 windows each -
 gas Q  averaging is 2M per window
 gas LJ averaging is 2M per window
 aq Q  averaging is 200M per window
 aq LJ averaging is 500M per window
These are the commands - 

../xFEPGAS20fQ Q
../xFEPGAS20bQ LJ
../xFEP200f20Q Q
../xFEP500b20Q LJ

The LJ FEPs are done in the growing direction for better acccuracy,
see: JCTC 2019, 15, 3941-3948. 

When finished, the 4 results can be extracted via

xGETDG molecule

delGhyd = aq (Q + LJ) - gas (Q + LJ)

Results are provided for ethanol. Only the sumout files have been retained.

xGETDG etoh

delGhyd = -1.105 -0.135 -5.972 + 2.604 = -4.608 kcal/mol (expt = -5.00)

